        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Flavin, Peter Benchley, George Archainbaud, Beulah Marie Dix\n- Works: Three Who Loved\n- Topics: American literature, film\n\nFacts:\n- Martin Archer Flavin was born on November 2, 1883, and was an American playwright and novelist.\n- Three Who Loved is a 1931 American Pre-Code drama film.\n- Three Who Loved was directed by George Archainbaud.\n- Three Who Loved was written from a screenplay by Beulah Marie Dix.\n- Three Who Loved was based on a story by Pulitzer Prize-winning author Martin Flavin.\n- Peter Bradford Benchley was born on May 8, 1940, and was an American author and screenwriter.\n- Martin Archer Flavin died on December 27, 1967.\n- Peter Bradford Benchley died on February 11, 2006.",
